{
  "$comment": "Search operations that also get a success-path test sending page.limit and a sort, asserting at most `limit` items and, when checkOrder is true, items ordered by the sort field. checkOrder is only true for timestamp fields: their ISO-8601 values order the same in JavaScript as on the server, while names depend on the database collation. searchCatalogAssets and searchWorkspaces also send a filter (name exists), since no other success test of theirs does. Each search also gets a page-offset test (page.from = offsetFrom) that, where the order is checked, compares its items with the same slice of an unpaged query. The order test sends the opposite sort too and expects the opposite order, so a server that ignores sort cannot pass.",
  "limit": 2,
  "offsetFrom": 1,
  "searches": [
    {
      "operationId": "searchCatalogAssets",
      "sort": {
        "field": "created",
        "order": "DESC"
      },
      "checkOrder": true,
      "filter": {
        "name": {
          "$exists": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "operationId": "searchCatalogAssetFileUsages",
      "sort": {
        "field": "name",
        "order": "ASC"
      },
      "checkOrder": false
    },
    {
